896 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Proverbs 4:7 says wisdom is supreme; therefore get wisdom. Though it costs all you have, get understanding \(NIV\). The Word of God is unequivocal about the fact that without wisdom, one is hopeless, no matter what else one has. In everything God does, He operates with wisdom. Our revelation of God is not complete until we emphasise the wisdom dimension of Him.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
897 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The first thing that comes to mind when the average person thinks about God is how powerful He is, to do all He does. Truly, God is great in power and He desires His people to know and reveal His power. Have you ever wondered how wise God must be to do all He does? This tendency to lean towards celebrating power over wisdom is not because God has demonstrated more of His power than His wisdom, rather it is because humans by default, seem to attach more importance to the demonstration of power other than that of wisdom. Thus, if a person divides a sea supernaturally, passes through and closes it behind himself, leaving others behind, humans would for ever look at such a person in awe. However, if another taps into innovation and creativity to design and construct a bridge, opening a pathway for others to cross after him, he may not receive as much admiration as the first person even though what the second person has done is more beneficial to the people and enduring than the first. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
898 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (31 WISDOM KEYS)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
899 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This is to say that we must learn to place high value and honour for the demonstration of wisdom.)
/E (This is to say that we must learn to place high value and honour for the demonstration of wisdom.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
900 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Oftentimes, power manifests by breaking natural laws, while wisdom manifests by riding on natural occurrences. However, we must know that both wisdom and power are the greatness of God in operation. Power and wisdom are both divine attributes that complement each other in the operations of God and as a child of God, you can and should have both. Thus, Jeremiah 10:12 says, God has made the earth by His power, He has established the world by His wisdom and has stretched out the heavens at His discretion \(NKJV\). God made the universe as a display of both His wisdom and power. Thus, Christ is revealed as both the power of God and the Wisdom of God \(1 Corinthians 1:24\).)
/E (Oftentimes, power manifests by breaking natural laws, while wisdom manifests by riding on natural occurrences. However, we must know that both wisdom and power are the greatness of God in operation. Power and wisdom are both divine attributes that complement each other in the operations of God and as a child of God, you can and should have both. Thus, Jeremiah 10:12 says, God has made the earth by His power, He has established the world by His wisdom and has stretched out the heavens at His discretion \(NKJV\). God made the universe as a display of both His wisdom and power. Thus, Christ is revealed as both the power of God and the Wisdom of God \(1 Corinthians 1:24\).)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
