1004 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (THE WIDOM OF ORDER)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1005 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (While it is true that the Holy Spirit might break or disrupt human order when He starts moving, He is not an enemy of order. The Holy Spirit loves order and many times, might even demand for order to be in place before He blesses or moves upon something.)
/E (While it is true that the Holy Spirit might break or disrupt human order when He starts moving, He is not an enemy of order. The Holy Spirit loves order and many times, might even demand for order to be in place before He blesses or moves upon something.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1006 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The book of Numbers is an Old Testament classic on order. God ordered the position where everything was to be put. He specified the dressing for every priest and for every person that was to carry out a task for Him. He was clear on who was in charge of every assignment and gadget in the Tabernacle and in the entire nation of Israel. He gave details on where each tribe was to camp and who was to move first when they were to start a journey and those to stop first when it was time to rest. God left nothing to chance, He gave sitting arrangement, dressing arrangement, movement instructions, allocated tasks, responsibility and position and insisted that everyone do what they are supposed to do without breaking order. God is obsessed with order. Living an orderly life is Godlikeness.)
/E (The book of Numbers is an Old Testament classic on order. God ordered the position where everything was to be put. He specified the dressing for every priest and for every person that was to carry out a task for Him. He was clear on who was in charge of every assignment and gadget in the Tabernacle and in the entire nation of Israel. He gave details on where each tribe was to camp and who was to move first when they were to start a journey and those to stop first when it was time to rest. God left nothing to chance, He gave sitting arrangement, dressing arrangement, movement instructions, allocated tasks, responsibility and position and insisted that everyone do what they are supposed to do without breaking order. God is obsessed with order. Living an orderly life is Godlikeness.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1007 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Another striking order in the Book of Number is the orderly documentation of every fact. The details with which the statistics of the civilization which lived thousands of year were recorded and kept till date shows that order is a divine wisdom that only God gives and is not necessarily acquired through school education. Many educated individuals and organisations do not have the level of facts, figures and statistics that the primitive nation of Israel provided and preserved till date about all the records and details of their nation and journey. Truly, order is a God-given wisdom and is not merely human taught. This is why it is right to pray for the wisdom to be orderly in all areas of life.)
/E (Another striking order in the Book of Number is the orderly documentation of every fact. The details with which the statistics of the civilization which lived thousands of year were recorded and kept till date shows that order is a divine wisdom that only God gives and is not necessarily acquired through school education. Many educated individuals and organisations do not have the level of facts, figures and statistics that the primitive nation of Israel provided and preserved till date about all the records and details of their nation and journey. Truly, order is a God-given wisdom and is not merely human taught. This is why it is right to pray for the wisdom to be orderly in all areas of life.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
