/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1954 0 R
/ActualText (When Paul was called, he first wanted to start public manifestation immediately but he met resistance. In fact, even without resistance, he might not have had the level of success he eventually had. This is because the resistance and persecution he experienced made him retreat to Arabia and later to Damascus. He also spent some time in his hometown Tarsus and later in Antioch where he spent years praying and growing alongside some other people \(Acts 13:2\). It was after many years of his conversion that he was eventually commissioned by God into the ministry. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3]
>>
