1050 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1955 0 R
/ActualText (The next mention about Jesus after the stories surrounding His birth was when He was twelve years. Thereafter, He was in oblivion till he was thirty years. This season was definitely not idled away; it was spent in diligent preparation. When Jesus showed up on the scene at the age of thirty, He was baptised and the Holy Spirit came upon Him. Immediately, after being filled with the Holy Spirit, he was again led by the Spirit into the wilderness where he was alone in the wilderness for 40 days and nights and there had encounters that chartered His destiny and ministry. The concept of being alone to have life and destiny encounters is an indisputable trend in the scripture.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
