1058 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Wisdom is required in building anything commendable. Prov. 24: 3 says, through skillful and godly wisdom is a house \(a life, a home, a family, an enterprise, a business, a ministry, an organisation\) built, and by understanding it is established \(on a sound and good foundation\).)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1059 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (\(AMP Version, some additions, mine\). Anywhere you see anything well built, wisdom was employed. Wisdom is justified by what it builds. If you want to build anything that men will see and commend, you must be intentional about using wisdom. .)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1060 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In 1 Cor. 3: 10, Paul says, by the grace given to me, I laid a foundation as a wise builder, and someone else is building on it. But each one should build with care. The level of wisdom of a person can be determined by the quality of what he has built or is building with his or her life. Do not just live from day to day, let the daily activities of your life be cumulative in building something specific. Whatever you are building must be related to your goals. Your activities, time, resources investment and spiritual/mental exertion must revolve round what you are building. You must go through life with the mindset of a builder.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1061 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The following are things to build with your lifetime:)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1062 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Build a relationship with God: Good relationships do not just happen, they are deliberately built. Time is a major ingredient for building a relationship. Another key component in building a good relationship is prioritisation. )
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [5]
>>
