1161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Growth is one of the most powerful mysteries of life. One of the wisest decisions one can make is to be committed to continual growth in every area of life. There are untold potentials and opportunities available to anyone who keeps growing. The egg in the womb of a woman is fertilised and with growth, it becomes a sophisticated human being who manufactures jet engines, designs complex computer systems and sits as executive over a board of conglomerates, multinationals and national organisations. Growth is the difference between little and great. Thus, Matt 13: 31 explains that the Kingdom of Heaven is like a mustard seed which a man took and sowed in his field, which is indeed the least of all the seeds; but when it is grown it is greater than the herbs and becomes a tree, so that the birds of the air come and nest in its branches. \(NKJV\).)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
