/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (God says, I am the Lord, and I do not change . . .  A quality of God is that He does not change. The flip side of this statement is that the quality of man is change. The reason God does not change is not because He detests change, but because He does not need to. God has factored all things from eternity past, present and future into view before He acts, speaks or decides, so, He will never need to change who He is, what He did or what He said.)
/E (God says, I am the Lord, and I do not change . . .  A quality of God is that He does not change. The flip side of this statement is that the quality of man is change. The reason God does not change is not because He detests change, but because He does not need to. God has factored all things from eternity past, present and future into view before He acts, speaks or decides, so, He will never need to change who He is, what He did or what He said.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [0]
>>
