1271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (One of the best decisions you can ever make in your lifetime is the decision to be rich, backed up with corresponding actions. Poverty is one of the greatest limitations in life. Poverty makes a wise person look foolish and riches have the ability to make a foolish person be accepted as wise. Is it possible to be wise and poor? Absolutely! We have established that there are many streams of wisdom and that it is not all of them that is financial in its expression. When someone has all other streams of wisdom in place but lacks financial wisdom to generate financial results, even all the other streams of wisdom he has is despised by people. The Bible gives the account of a city that was under siege by an enemy-army and a poor, wise man knew how to save the town, and so it was rescued. But afterward no one thought to thank him. So even though wisdom is better than strength, those who are wise will be despised if they are poor. What they say will not be appreciated for long \(Eccl 9:15-16\))
/Pg 81 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A wise man who is poor may eventually suffer the same fate with a fool. This is the reason it is wisdom to insist on your wisdom translating to financial wealth. Do all righteously possible and rise up to pay the necessary prices to make sure your knowledge, wisdom, education, gifts, capacity and spirituality translate to wealth in a godly way.)
/Pg 81 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Wealth is not age, race, gender or religion sensitive. It answers to the person who follows the laws of wealth. )
/Pg 81 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (64)
/Pg 81 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
