<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Law of Giving seems to be a universally accepted law. Nearly all religions, beliefs, schools of thoughts and philosophies believe in the noble idea of giving. Thus, Christians and people of other religions, atheists, humanists, business executives and even sometimes criminals somehow somewhere believe giving is one of the displays of humanity at his best. Perhaps, one of the most popular scriptures in Christianity is John 3:16, For God loved the world so much that he gave his one and only Son, so that everyone who believes in him will not perish but have eternal life. Giving is the heart of Christianity and the heart of God.)
/Pg 85 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
