<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Giving is like sowing a seed to receive its harvest, so, it is he that sows that reaps the harvest of what he has sown. Prov. 11:24 explains, "There are those who [generously] scatter abroad, and yet increase more; there are those who withhold more than is fitting or what is justly due, but it results only in want." \(AMP\) A giver is like a sower who scatters his seed on good soil, and then watches the seeds grow into a forest of fruitful vines. A non-giver is like one hold onto his seeds and eats them up. When harvest time comes, there is nothing to eat again. Shying away from giving hence, leads to poverty and lack. )
/E (Giving is like sowing a seed to receive its harvest, so, it is he that sows that reaps the harvest of what he has sown. Prov. 11:24 explains, "There are those who [generously] scatter abroad, and yet increase more; there are those who withhold more than is fitting or what is justly due, but it results only in want." \(AMP\) A giver is like a sower who scatters his seed on good soil, and then watches the seeds grow into a forest of fruitful vines. A non-giver is like one hold onto his seeds and eats them up. When harvest time comes, there is nothing to eat again. Shying away from giving hence, leads to poverty and lack. )
