<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (A last note on the wisdom of giving: extremely prosperous and wealthy people in the Kingdom are those who don't just give when it is convenient, but give even when it is inconvenient like Abraham who was willing to give his precious son Isaac as a sacrifice when demanded by God \(Gen.22:2\). People who love nothing more than their relationship with God and would willingly give up everything and anything for God are the ones God will entrust with the true riches of His Kingdom. In other words, it does not just matter that you give, how much you give matters. Thus, 2 Cor 9: 6 says "But this I say, He which soweth sparingly shall reap also sparingly; and he which soweth bountifully shall reap also bountifully." Note that the true value of your giving is not in how much you give, but how much is left after you give.)
/E (A last note on the wisdom of giving: extremely prosperous and wealthy people in the Kingdom are those who don't just give when it is convenient, but give even when it is inconvenient like Abraham who was willing to give his precious son Isaac as a sacrifice when demanded by God \(Gen.22:2\). People who love nothing more than their relationship with God and would willingly give up everything and anything for God are the ones God will entrust with the true riches of His Kingdom. In other words, it does not just matter that you give, how much you give matters. Thus, 2 Cor 9: 6 says "But this I say, He which soweth sparingly shall reap also sparingly; and he which soweth bountifully shall reap also bountifully." Note that the true value of your giving is not in how much you give, but how much is left after you give.)
