<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Bible in Prov. 1:5 says: "A wise man will hear, and will increase learning; and a man of understanding shall attain unto wise counsels." This is to say that a wise man is one who gives his ears to hearing, so as to increase his learning. The scripture here, measures one's wisdom by one's openness to listen and learn. Learning is not a passive experience; it is an intentional act of yielding and receiving. In Acts 7:22, the Bible says: "And Moses was learned in all the wisdom of the Egyptians, and was mighty in words and in deeds." This scripture here as well, measures one's might by learning.)
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [2]
>>
