1343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Apostle Paul was writing to his son in the Lord and mentee, Timothy, in \(2Tim. 2:15\) "Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth." Learning gives you confidence and keeps your chin up when you stand in any gathering. And in a case of a person who has been schooled into heresy and wrong doctrine; reordering such person unto rightness is still through learning. So, it is of a surety, that as one grows through life, there will always be the need to learn, unlearn and learn; having no shame for corrections. Apostle Paul further exhorts in \(2Tim. 3:14\) "But continue thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them" This is a call for continuity in learning, but only in a doctrine which has been proven and is true, as backed up by the integrity of the one from who one learns. So, it is not just to learn, but to also assess and discern the uprightness of the teacher, by appraising his track record of steadfastness and rectitude over time.)
/E (Apostle Paul was writing to his son in the Lord and mentee, Timothy, in \(2Tim. 2:15\) "Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth." Learning gives you confidence and keeps your chin up when you stand in any gathering. And in a case of a person who has been schooled into heresy and wrong doctrine; reordering such person unto rightness is still through learning. So, it is of a surety, that as one grows through life, there will always be the need to learn, unlearn and learn; having no shame for corrections. Apostle Paul further exhorts in \(2Tim. 3:14\) "But continue thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them" This is a call for continuity in learning, but only in a doctrine which has been proven and is true, as backed up by the integrity of the one from who one learns. So, it is not just to learn, but to also assess and discern the uprightness of the teacher, by appraising his track record of steadfastness and rectitude over time.)
