<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (From historical times, the world has seen the emergence of powerful leaders, with brilliant minds and skillful hands across various spheres of influence. These leaders were notable for their conquests, royalty, inventions, philosophies, business strategies, political policies, creative arts, military power, etc. They held the world in awe, for their indelible impacts on the sands of time; men revered them as gods on earth. But, sadly, in spite of their great achievements and successes, many of them failed to secure their great names in the stronghold of good character, and so, they were not worthy models.)
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Character is a virtue; the quality of being just and doing justice. Character is one's strength to adhere to principles that make for morality and integrity. The features of good character will define it more explicitly; truthfulness, uprightness, straightforwardness, authenticity, honesty, integrity, rectitude, temperance, humility, courage, faithfulness, sincerity, perseverance, etc. These and many other moral virtues are the indices to measure a person of good character.)
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
