1367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The Amplified version says "think on and weigh and take account of these things [fix your minds on them]" That is, keep them in your mind, meditate on them, let them become the underlying principles which defines your actions and reactions. The need to be a person of strong and upright character can never be overemphasized, the Bible is full of stories of men whose lack of good character cost them their birth rights, thrones, destines, fulfilments, and even their lives. These men struggled to keep up with the quality of being a person of good character, but they could not, and hence, their stories ended tragically. Even the wisest man that ever lived, who himself taught on the essence of good character in Proverbs 1:7a, "The fear of the Lord is the beginning of knowledge" could not hold on to his convictions till the end. This is what then gave rise to the notion of "no one is perfect, we are all humans, after all". So, men began to justify their wrongs with excuses of just being human, which may appear understandable and consolable, but the reign of corruption continues to extend across dispensations.)
/E (The Amplified version says "think on and weigh and take account of these things [fix your minds on them]" That is, keep them in your mind, meditate on them, let them become the underlying principles which defines your actions and reactions. The need to be a person of strong and upright character can never be overemphasized, the Bible is full of stories of men whose lack of good character cost them their birth rights, thrones, destines, fulfilments, and even their lives. These men struggled to keep up with the quality of being a person of good character, but they could not, and hence, their stories ended tragically. Even the wisest man that ever lived, who himself taught on the essence of good character in Proverbs 1:7a, "The fear of the Lord is the beginning of knowledge" could not hold on to his convictions till the end. This is what then gave rise to the notion of "no one is perfect, we are all humans, after all". So, men began to justify their wrongs with excuses of just being human, which may appear understandable and consolable, but the reign of corruption continues to extend across dispensations.)
