1387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Sadly, humility has been grossly misconceived and misunderstood to mean self-abasement, being cowardly and unconfident, or walking with heads and backs bowed in timidity and subservience. Another misconception in Christianity about being humble is that humility is a noble art of denying your strength and being over-conscious of your weaknesses. Humility is not living a low life with no aspiration for greatness. Jesus, the Most Humble did not mince words about declaring who He was and how great He was. When He told them that He was the Son of God, the Messiah that was to come, the One greater than Abraham, Solomon and all the prophets, they could not handle that level of boldness.)
/E (Sadly, humility has been grossly misconceived and misunderstood to mean self-abasement, being cowardly and unconfident, or walking with heads and backs bowed in timidity and subservience. Another misconception in Christianity about being humble is that humility is a noble art of denying your strength and being over-conscious of your weaknesses. Humility is not living a low life with no aspiration for greatness. Jesus, the Most Humble did not mince words about declaring who He was and how great He was. When He told them that He was the Son of God, the Messiah that was to come, the One greater than Abraham, Solomon and all the prophets, they could not handle that level of boldness.)
