/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Apostle Paul instructs in Phil. 2:3 "Let nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves." A humble person knows who he is and what he is capable of but still has high regards for one another, appreciating our own strengths, knowing they are given by God and at the same time, recognizing, appreciating and celebrating others for their uniqueness, and we should forbear one another in love and faith. A humble person is quick to transfer praise to others while a proud person has a voracious appetite for human praise.)
/E (Apostle Paul instructs in Phil. 2:3 "Let nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves." A humble person knows who he is and what he is capable of but still has high regards for one another, appreciating our own strengths, knowing they are given by God and at the same time, recognizing, appreciating and celebrating others for their uniqueness, and we should forbear one another in love and faith. A humble person is quick to transfer praise to others while a proud person has a voracious appetite for human praise.)
