1393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This is a sharp written verdict concerning God's primary judgement on the proud. That, it is God Himself who stands in the way of the proud, to impede his progress, for his end result will be to take the glory that belongs to God, and God will not let it happen. Then, the other end of the scripture explains how God empowers the humble unto progress and advancement in what he does, for God knows that, it is all unto His glory. In another scripture, it says that "God exalts the humble." \(1Pet. 5:6\) This and more shows how much God cherishes humility and the humble, and he is not afraid to elevate them, for they are carriers of His glory. Therefore, it is really wise to be humble.)
/E (This is a sharp written verdict concerning God's primary judgement on the proud. That, it is God Himself who stands in the way of the proud, to impede his progress, for his end result will be to take the glory that belongs to God, and God will not let it happen. Then, the other end of the scripture explains how God empowers the humble unto progress and advancement in what he does, for God knows that, it is all unto His glory. In another scripture, it says that "God exalts the humble." \(1Pet. 5:6\) This and more shows how much God cherishes humility and the humble, and he is not afraid to elevate them, for they are carriers of His glory. Therefore, it is really wise to be humble.)
