/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (If it is wisdom to honour, then it is foolishness to dishonour. Dishonour is the lack of recognition, condescension or pursuit of a grace or value that has the ability to add to you. To dishonour is to build a wall of barrier between you and what the person has to add to you. Dishonour is also sowing a seed, but a seed unto unproductivity, lack and lowliness. Whatever is dishonoured depreciates and whatever one does not honour cannot do one any good. Thus, nothing or no one can benefit you if you dishonour them in your heart. This is the reason many people are in a place and are not making headway there. You cannot dishonour your pastor, spouse, parent or boss in your heart and wonder why their presence is not benefiting you. Conversely, you cannot be a sustainable blessing to someone or in a place you are dishonoured. This is the reason it is wisdom to humbly withdraw from places and people where you are treated dishonourably as it would be mutually non-beneficial for such a relationship to continue. If I cannot benefit you since you dishonour me and I also depreciate because I am dishonoured, then both of us would lose in the relationship - it is better I walk away.)
/E (If it is wisdom to honour, then it is foolishness to dishonour. Dishonour is the lack of recognition, condescension or pursuit of a grace or value that has the ability to add to you. To dishonour is to build a wall of barrier between you and what the person has to add to you. Dishonour is also sowing a seed, but a seed unto unproductivity, lack and lowliness. Whatever is dishonoured depreciates and whatever one does not honour cannot do one any good. Thus, nothing or no one can benefit you if you dishonour them in your heart. This is the reason many people are in a place and are not making headway there. You cannot dishonour your pastor, spouse, parent or boss in your heart and wonder why their presence is not benefiting you. Conversely, you cannot be a sustainable blessing to someone or in a place you are dishonoured. This is the reason it is wisdom to humbly withdraw from places and people where you are treated dishonourably as it would be mutually non-beneficial for such a relationship to continue. If I cannot benefit you since you dishonour me and I also depreciate because I am dishonoured, then both of us would lose in the relationship - it is better I walk away.)
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
