/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The second level of honour is unto men. Among men, the first command of honour is to our parents - biological and spiritual. Ex. 20:12 "Honor your father and your mother, that your days may be long in the land that the Lord your God is giving you." Many people do not realise that honouring older people even when they are not your parents is also a scriptural command: 'You shall rise before the gray headed and honor the presence of an old man, and fear your God: I am the Lord. Lev 19:32)
/E (The second level of honour is unto men. Among men, the first command of honour is to our parents - biological and spiritual. Ex. 20:12 "Honor your father and your mother, that your days may be long in the land that the Lord your God is giving you." Many people do not realise that honouring older people even when they are not your parents is also a scriptural command: 'You shall rise before the gray headed and honor the presence of an old man, and fear your God: I am the Lord. Lev 19:32)
