1425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The way to reap honour is to sow it. For every seed of honour sown, there will be a harvest of honour. Also, we must conduct ourselves with honour so that we can be accorded due honour. It is wise to conduct ourselves, our businesses, our platforms and careers honourably so that people will look up to us and believe in us. Do you know that people only follow someone they honour? If they are following when there is no honour in their heart, they are merely acting up. So, in building honour, you have to pay attention to yourself. Have a good self-perception about yourself, be conscious of the values you have and carry yourself with high esteem and self-honour. The next thing is to pay attention to your affairs and dealings with people, in conversations, conduct and actions. Another thing is to give priority to your physical outlook, your grooming and appearance. You must be well packaged and branded. These are ways of building up yourself in honour, so that people can perceive you in that light and accord honour to you and to whatever you do.)
/E (The way to reap honour is to sow it. For every seed of honour sown, there will be a harvest of honour. Also, we must conduct ourselves with honour so that we can be accorded due honour. It is wise to conduct ourselves, our businesses, our platforms and careers honourably so that people will look up to us and believe in us. Do you know that people only follow someone they honour? If they are following when there is no honour in their heart, they are merely acting up. So, in building honour, you have to pay attention to yourself. Have a good self-perception about yourself, be conscious of the values you have and carry yourself with high esteem and self-honour. The next thing is to pay attention to your affairs and dealings with people, in conversations, conduct and actions. Another thing is to give priority to your physical outlook, your grooming and appearance. You must be well packaged and branded. These are ways of building up yourself in honour, so that people can perceive you in that light and accord honour to you and to whatever you do.)
/Pg 109 0 R
/K [1]
