1429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The relationships around you are an adequate measure and an accurate prediction of the level of your wisdom and the quality of your persona. People who have a good number of high quality persons as the reciprocal relationships in their immediate networks are those who have capacity and value themselves. If you want to have a fair guess at the quality of character, capacity, competence and value, check the reciprocal relationships in your life. A reciprocal relationship is one in which the person is interested in you and you are interested in them. A reciprocal relationship is not parasitic and is not one in which you are clinging to or pursuing someone who only does not know how to do away with you. A reciprocal relationship is a symbiotic relationship and there is mutual derivation of value and reciprocal respect.)
/Pg 110 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Great people do not spend time with nonentities. Thus, if you are in a network of 10 mediocre persons, you are the eleventh, no rocket science about that. One of the surest ways to change your life is to change your associations. Proverbs 13:20 says, He that walks with wise men shall be wise: but a companion of fools shall be destroyed. The person who associates with the great stands a great chance to be great.)
/Pg 110 0 R
/K [2]
>>
