/T (Good parents seek to lay up an inheritance for their children. Prov. 13:22 says, a good man leaveth an inheritance to his children's children . . Vital inheritances to leave include a spiritual heritage of knowledge and love for God, a legacy of a good name and goodwill as well as material and financial estates. Laying up inheritance for children is a deliberate effort that takes diligence and sacrifice. This includes living in a way that your life, achievement and the name you have earned poses an advantage to your children in the future. )
