1473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Sometimes, silence is the greatest expression of wisdom. A young boy was shown a picture of his enviable future. He woke up from his sleep, perplexed, he couldn't understand nor read meaning to this baffling vision he saw. In his restlessness, he couldn't keep the door of his mouth; his naivety and curiosity drove him to his elder brothers, he narrated his dream to them, and they, being elderly could deduce that his dream is supposed to be a prophecy of his future superiority over. They hated him, envied and despised him. This young boy unwittingly opened up himself to a life of loneliness, rejection and persecution because he was void of wisdom at that time. \(see Genesis 37:1-11\) Very few things are more foolish and more devastating in life than telling things about yourself to a person\(s\) that you are not supposed to. The Wisdom of Secrecy is an advanced course in the school of wisdom.)
/E (Sometimes, silence is the greatest expression of wisdom. A young boy was shown a picture of his enviable future. He woke up from his sleep, perplexed, he couldn't understand nor read meaning to this baffling vision he saw. In his restlessness, he couldn't keep the door of his mouth; his naivety and curiosity drove him to his elder brothers, he narrated his dream to them, and they, being elderly could deduce that his dream is supposed to be a prophecy of his future superiority over. They hated him, envied and despised him. This young boy unwittingly opened up himself to a life of loneliness, rejection and persecution because he was void of wisdom at that time. \(see Genesis 37:1-11\) Very few things are more foolish and more devastating in life than telling things about yourself to a person\(s\) that you are not supposed to. The Wisdom of Secrecy is an advanced course in the school of wisdom.)
/Pg 119 0 R
/K [1]
