1499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (It is wisdom to keep quiet when you should keep quiet and it is wisdom to speak when you should speak. Knowing the what, when and how of making utterance correctly is one of the highest indices of wisdom. You must make it an ambition to always know what to say and the right time to say it. People have gotten into trouble by what they said even more than by what they did. Utterance, many times, implicates people more than actions.)
/E (It is wisdom to keep quiet when you should keep quiet and it is wisdom to speak when you should speak. Knowing the what, when and how of making utterance correctly is one of the highest indices of wisdom. You must make it an ambition to always know what to say and the right time to say it. People have gotten into trouble by what they said even more than by what they did. Utterance, many times, implicates people more than actions.)
/Pg 123 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Words are actually meant to be for communication and also to disseminate information, but it is not everything that is meant to be verbalised. Silence, gesture, countenance, disposition are all forms of communication. So wisdom of utterance is knowing what type of utterance is best at a particular time.)
/E (Words are actually meant to be for communication and also to disseminate information, but it is not everything that is meant to be verbalised. Silence, gesture, countenance, disposition are all forms of communication. So wisdom of utterance is knowing what type of utterance is best at a particular time.)
/Pg 123 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (For an intention to be verbalized, utterances have to be made. So verbalisation is crucial in communication. Thus, maximise your right and freedom to speak, but understand that one can either speak his way to life or speak his way to death. Prov. 18: 21 says, Death and Life are in the power of the tongue, and those who love it will eat its fruit. The truth is that people speak, but only few speak as guided by the wisdom of utterance. The wisdom of utterance is the wisdom to know what to say, when to speak, how to present it, to whom to speak to/with and if need be, when to keep silent.)
/E (For an intention to be verbalized, utterances have to be made. So verbalisation is crucial in communication. Thus, maximise your right and freedom to speak, but understand that one can either speak his way to life or speak his way to death. Prov. 18: 21 says, Death and Life are in the power of the tongue, and those who love it will eat its fruit. The truth is that people speak, but only few speak as guided by the wisdom of utterance. The wisdom of utterance is the wisdom to know what to say, when to speak, how to present it, to whom to speak to/with and if need be, when to keep silent.)
/Pg 123 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
