1504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (It is also important to know that Satan, demons and wicked people do not know so much about you; they mostly depend on your utterance to deduce facts about you. So, make it your commitment to keep them clueless about your destiny and situations by relying completely on the Holy Spirit to be the gatekeeper of your mouth, and let the Word of God be your default utterance at the face of occurrences.)
/E (It is also important to know that Satan, demons and wicked people do not know so much about you; they mostly depend on your utterance to deduce facts about you. So, make it your commitment to keep them clueless about your destiny and situations by relying completely on the Holy Spirit to be the gatekeeper of your mouth, and let the Word of God be your default utterance at the face of occurrences.)
/Pg 124 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This Wisdom of utterance is the ability to speak the right words at the right time, and present your utterances in the right manner. Proverbs 16:23 \(AMP\) says, the mind of the wise instructs his mouth, and adds learning and persuasiveness to his lips. This shows that a wise person does not just speak because he feels like speaking or he is asked to, he speaks only as instructed by spiritual, emotional and mental intelligence. Always intelligently weigh the consequences of your utterances before you make them. A wise person knows the consequence of every utterance and only speaks for intended consequence.)
/E (This Wisdom of utterance is the ability to speak the right words at the right time, and present your utterances in the right manner. Proverbs 16:23 \(AMP\) says, the mind of the wise instructs his mouth, and adds learning and persuasiveness to his lips. This shows that a wise person does not just speak because he feels like speaking or he is asked to, he speaks only as instructed by spiritual, emotional and mental intelligence. Always intelligently weigh the consequences of your utterances before you make them. A wise person knows the consequence of every utterance and only speaks for intended consequence.)
/Pg 124 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Another key component of the Wisdom of Utterance is speaking boldly when you need to. Declaring spiritual words over physical realities is spiritual wisdom. You should not keep your mouth closed in spiritual warfare. Putting the Word of God on your lips and declaring it boldly in the face of contrary is wisdom. If Satan, situations or the enemy says anything contrary to you, it is not wisdom to keep quiet. Decree back what you want to see, that daring utterance is wisdom. In spiritual warfare, utterance is a necessity. Discretion in speech is needed before men but in the realms of the spirit, the wisdom of utterance is demonstrated by bold speaking and daring declarations. Ultimately, the utterance is only available through yielding to the Holy Spirit. The Holy Spirit prompts you on when to speak and when to be quiet.)
/E (Another key component of the Wisdom of Utterance is speaking boldly when you need to. Declaring spiritual words over physical realities is spiritual wisdom. You should not keep your mouth closed in spiritual warfare. Putting the Word of God on your lips and declaring it boldly in the face of contrary is wisdom. If Satan, situations or the enemy says anything contrary to you, it is not wisdom to keep quiet. Decree back what you want to see, that daring utterance is wisdom. In spiritual warfare, utterance is a necessity. Discretion in speech is needed before men but in the realms of the spirit, the wisdom of utterance is demonstrated by bold speaking and daring declarations. Ultimately, the utterance is only available through yielding to the Holy Spirit. The Holy Spirit prompts you on when to speak and when to be quiet.)
/Pg 124 0 R
/K [2]
>>
