1554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (There are some practices that are doses to live a happy and healthy life. These habits power up and secure a life of bliss, strength and hope. One of such practice is living a lifestyle of immense gratitude for every gift of life. Gratitude is an act that begins from a heart that recognizes a blessing, and then responds to that blessing by acknowledgement and appreciation. Grateful people are thoughtful people, who will look for a reason to give thanks, even in a seeming unpleasant situation, rather than being encumbered with worries and complaints. In positive psychology research, gratitude is strongly and consistently associated with greater happiness. Gratitude helps people feel more positive emotions, relish good experiences, improve their health, deal with adversity, and build strong relationships. Grateful people live under an atmosphere of hope, which make them immune to any dart of sorrow and grief life throws at them. A grateful person is not just grateful because every line is falling in right places; but even when things seem not to go as planned, they have a beautiful sigh of "it is well." to express. Gratitude stems from a depth of understanding that is rooted in the knowledge of God's goodness.)
/E (There are some practices that are doses to live a happy and healthy life. These habits power up and secure a life of bliss, strength and hope. One of such practice is living a lifestyle of immense gratitude for every gift of life. Gratitude is an act that begins from a heart that recognizes a blessing, and then responds to that blessing by acknowledgement and appreciation. Grateful people are thoughtful people, who will look for a reason to give thanks, even in a seeming unpleasant situation, rather than being encumbered with worries and complaints. In positive psychology research, gratitude is strongly and consistently associated with greater happiness. Gratitude helps people feel more positive emotions, relish good experiences, improve their health, deal with adversity, and build strong relationships. Grateful people live under an atmosphere of hope, which make them immune to any dart of sorrow and grief life throws at them. A grateful person is not just grateful because every line is falling in right places; but even when things seem not to go as planned, they have a beautiful sigh of "it is well." to express. Gratitude stems from a depth of understanding that is rooted in the knowledge of God's goodness.)
/Pg 132 0 R
