/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (God is good and rich unto all, but He is unapologetically gracious to people who have mastered the art of thanking Him for every little thing in their lives. In the Bible, there are many cases of people whose lifestyle of gratitude to God made them highly preferred above their peers, prolonged their lives, multiplied their resources, fortified their camps and engendered God's power to turn hopeless situation around. One of such occurrences is seen in the book of 2Chronicles 20: 1-25 "\(vs. 21:\) And when he had consulted with the people, he appointed singers unto the Lord, and that should praise the beauty of holiness, as they went out before the army, and to say, Praise the Lord; for his mercy endureth for ever." In a situation that seems defeat and destruction is imminent, the wisdom of gratitude teaches to look away from the tempestuous wind of life and set one's gaze on Jesus only, giving thanks and reassuring oneself of His steadfast love and unfailing mercy.)
/E (God is good and rich unto all, but He is unapologetically gracious to people who have mastered the art of thanking Him for every little thing in their lives. In the Bible, there are many cases of people whose lifestyle of gratitude to God made them highly preferred above their peers, prolonged their lives, multiplied their resources, fortified their camps and engendered God's power to turn hopeless situation around. One of such occurrences is seen in the book of 2Chronicles 20: 1-25 "\(vs. 21:\) And when he had consulted with the people, he appointed singers unto the Lord, and that should praise the beauty of holiness, as they went out before the army, and to say, Praise the Lord; for his mercy endureth for ever." In a situation that seems defeat and destruction is imminent, the wisdom of gratitude teaches to look away from the tempestuous wind of life and set one's gaze on Jesus only, giving thanks and reassuring oneself of His steadfast love and unfailing mercy.)
