/T (Prayer stems from an understanding that even though nothing works unless somebody is working on it, there is also the need for a supernatural intervention that empowers one to sow and reap, even a hundredfold. Prayer is a conscious partnership with a spirit to bless the work of one's hands and multiply the results those hands produce. Wisdom principles are not substitutes for prayer; it is also wisdom to pray. And to balance up the square, prayer is also not a substitute for wisdom principles. Prayer is as well a wisdom principle as the others, and it is chiefly positioned because, it is not just a principle to add on )
