1578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Jesus Christ was not just a passionate advocate of prayer; he practically lived a life of prayer, in building up HIMSELF, his MINISTRY and setting OTHERS into purpose and fulfilment. "And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed." \(Mk. 1:35\) Jesus devoted an ample part of his time to prayers, setting himself apart in solitude to build up himself, and to receive divine revelations and instructions from God, on what to do per time and season. So, prayer will first of all build you up, and then equip and empower you to build your life, destiny and vision. Men who are built up by prayer become strong and able men, who live above every limitation, brought down every stronghold of darkness and wrought great exploits as victors and conquerors. Men who pray, consistently evolve into the better version of themselves; for every second spent in prayer is an investment unto betterment, increase and expansion. The Bible clearly captured it in Jude 1:26 \(Amp\), "But you, beloved, build yourselves up [founded] on your most holy faith [make progress, rise like an edifice higher and higher], praying in the Holy Spirit;" Prayer is a builder. As one prays in the building language of the Spirit; there is constantly an upgrade. A small and fearful person can pray up himself into a strong giant, to do valiantly, and function in various dimensions of graces, as unlocked by prayers.)
/E (Jesus Christ was not just a passionate advocate of prayer; he practically lived a life of prayer, in building up HIMSELF, his MINISTRY and setting OTHERS into purpose and fulfilment. "And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed." \(Mk. 1:35\) Jesus devoted an ample part of his time to prayers, setting himself apart in solitude to build up himself, and to receive divine revelations and instructions from God, on what to do per time and season. So, prayer will first of all build you up, and then equip and empower you to build your life, destiny and vision. Men who are built up by prayer become strong and able men, who live above every limitation, brought down every stronghold of darkness and wrought great exploits as victors and conquerors. Men who pray, consistently evolve into the better version of themselves; for every second spent in prayer is an investment unto betterment, increase and expansion. The Bible clearly captured it in Jude 1:26 \(Amp\), "But you, beloved, build yourselves up [founded] on your most holy faith [make progress, rise like an edifice higher and higher], praying in the Holy Spirit;" Prayer is a builder. As one prays in the building language of the Spirit; there is constantly an upgrade. A small and fearful person can pray up himself into a strong giant, to do valiantly, and function in various dimensions of graces, as unlocked by prayers.)
