1583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (And lastly, prayer sets up others into the discoveries of their purpose in God, and preserves them unto fulfilment. A person can pray another into the Will of God for their lives, insisting on the salvation of their souls and that they should respond to their high callings in God. This prayer is called the prayer of intercession; standing in gap for others to set them up for a life of godliness and glory. There is a portion in the scriptures that portrays intercession as an act of God's Love and mercy to restore men unto himself, by raising up other men to stand in gap for them. "I have set watchmen upon thy walls, O Jerusalem, which shall never hold their peace day nor night: ye that make mention of the Lord, keep not silence. And give him no rest, till he establish, and till he make Jerusalem a praise in the earth." \(Isa. 62:6-7\))
