/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (In the Old Testament, three categories of people were anointed over the nation of Israel: the king, the priests and the prophet. The king and priest provide executive, judicial and legislative leadership while the prophet provided spiritual leadership. The nation experienced blessings when the king submitted to the spiritual fatherhood and authority of a genuine prophet of God. The country experienced problems when the king rebelled against the instructions and spiritual cover of the prophet. The spiritual is superior to the natural. It does not matter your position in the natural, there must be a fountain of spiritual blessings that speaks over your life.)
/E (In the Old Testament, three categories of people were anointed over the nation of Israel: the king, the priests and the prophet. The king and priest provide executive, judicial and legislative leadership while the prophet provided spiritual leadership. The nation experienced blessings when the king submitted to the spiritual fatherhood and authority of a genuine prophet of God. The country experienced problems when the king rebelled against the instructions and spiritual cover of the prophet. The spiritual is superior to the natural. It does not matter your position in the natural, there must be a fountain of spiritual blessings that speaks over your life.)
/Pg 142 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1602 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (At certain points in the history of Israel, Samuel was Prophet over the nation. He released prophetic blessings over Saul as king and as long as the king submitted to his fatherhood and blessings, he reigned in prosperity. After Saul rebelled against his prophetic cover, God led Samuel to place the prophetic blessing on David. David lived his entire life under the prophetic blessing and fatherly covering. At a point when Saul was after his life, he ran to meet his spiritual father in Ramah.)
