1619 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Classically, there are three orders of event in a man's life: his birth, his death and the life he lived in between; which then decides the life he would live after death. All through different ages and dispensations, ample and apt exegesis has been done on time and living in time. There are beautiful pieces of literature crafted by philosophers and theorists in a bid to define and give meaning to the verity of time and the reality of living. However, there hasn't been clarity and actual understanding of the essence of the life lived in time and of how it affects the life lived after time. And is it even true that there is some life after death? If there is, where is that location? How do we go there? What do we do there? What's it all about? These and many more are the myriad of questions asked by the inquisitive minds of men, but only project further confusions, because both the "what and how" of it is purely spiritual, and can be conceived and understood only by a spiritual mind. These vagueness and confusion is what the wisdom of eternity will by the Spirit, bring to light.)
/E (Classically, there are three orders of event in a man's life: his birth, his death and the life he lived in between; which then decides the life he would live after death. All through different ages and dispensations, ample and apt exegesis has been done on time and living in time. There are beautiful pieces of literature crafted by philosophers and theorists in a bid to define and give meaning to the verity of time and the reality of living. However, there hasn't been clarity and actual understanding of the essence of the life lived in time and of how it affects the life lived after time. And is it even true that there is some life after death? If there is, where is that location? How do we go there? What do we do there? What's it all about? These and many more are the myriad of questions asked by the inquisitive minds of men, but only project further confusions, because both the "what and how" of it is purely spiritual, and can be conceived and understood only by a spiritual mind. These vagueness and confusion is what the wisdom of eternity will by the Spirit, bring to light.)
