/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This is to say that eternity is an infinite space that exists outside the circumference of time. It is a reality that cannot be measured by and in time. In comparison, time is a measurable and finite existence that is marked within the infinite and immeasurable existence called eternity. So, we can rightly deduce that man is a being set out of eternity to live in time for a definite period, and then having lived in time should exit out of time to continue into eternity. To come into time, is by being born to live for a while in time, and then to exit out of time through an event called death. So, since man is a being set out of eternity by God to live in time, then there will surely be a continuation of man's existence after his life in time, and that; is his return to God in eternity. This therefore justifies the reality of life after death.)
/E (This is to say that eternity is an infinite space that exists outside the circumference of time. It is a reality that cannot be measured by and in time. In comparison, time is a measurable and finite existence that is marked within the infinite and immeasurable existence called eternity. So, we can rightly deduce that man is a being set out of eternity to live in time for a definite period, and then having lived in time should exit out of time to continue into eternity. To come into time, is by being born to live for a while in time, and then to exit out of time through an event called death. So, since man is a being set out of eternity by God to live in time, then there will surely be a continuation of man's existence after his life in time, and that; is his return to God in eternity. This therefore justifies the reality of life after death.)
