/T (The wisdom of eternity then teaches us to know that there is a direct implication of the life lived by man in time on the life man will live after time. A man's life should not just be lived as he wills nor as he pleases, but according to the will and for the pleasure of He who set him in time. This then explains the concept of purpose; that man does not just exist in time only to die after some while, but that man should live only to fulfil the purpose of why he exists in time.)
